Category 10,  Topic 23
Message 81        Sat Mar 26, 1988
G.BAILEY1 [ATHENA]           at 13:26 PST
              
Lee, your proposal (known as TP88-038) is in the pile for consideration at the
May TC meeting, and I will state your request to postpone its consideration as
a motion to commit it to the group that is working on control structure and
looping issues.  We will probably convene that group at least once in
Rochester and it is probable that this group will not have concrete
recommendations for some time.  Unfortunately, it is difficult to indicate
your willingness to accept the FORTH-79 definition in our audit trail and
unless SOMEONE generates a proposal to that effect there is no way it can even
be considered.  If you consider the FORTH-79 loop behavior to be equally
desirable, there is absolutely nothing wrong with submitting a separate
proposal to that effect.  There are plentiful cases where a submitter finds
two mutually exclusive changes equally acceptable, and in such a case two
proposals are easier to work with than would be a single proposal outlining
two possibilities.  Cheers - Greg.


